          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>During START triage, you open a casualty's airway but they still do not breathe.</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>During START triage, you open a casualty's airway but they still do not breathe. What colour do you tag them?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Red — immediate</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Red is reserved for casualties who are breathing but at a rate above 30 per minute, or who fail the perfusion or mental status checks. A casualty who remains apnoeic after airway opening is tagged black, not red.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Yellow — delayed</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Yellow is for casualties who are breathing, perfusing, and able to obey a simple command, but are not the most urgent. Absent breathing after airway opening is tagged black.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Green — minor</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Green is for the walking wounded who moved to the designated area in the first triage step. A casualty who is not breathing is far from minor — they are tagged black.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Black — deceased/expectant</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. In START triage, a casualty who does not breathe even after the airway is opened is tagged black. This reflects the mass casualty principle of directing limited resources to those most likely to survive with timely treatment.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The correct answer is black. In START triage, if the casualty still does not breathe after you open the airway, they are tagged black, not red or yellow."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct — no breathing after airway opening is tagged black under START triage."
                }
              ],
